    "steps": [
      "Whisk together the flour, turmeric, and salt, then cut in the cold butter with a pastry cutter or your fingers until the mixture resembles coarse crumbs.",
      "Add the ice water a little at a time, mixing just until a firm dough comes together. Shape into a disc, wrap, and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes.",
      "Meanwhile, make the filling: heat the vegetable oil in a skillet over medium heat and cook the onion, garlic, and scotch bonnet pepper until softened, about 4 minutes.",
      "Add the ground beef and cook, breaking it up with a spoon, until browned, about 6-8 minutes.",
      "Stir in the green onion, thyme, allspice, curry powder, and black pepper and cook for 1 minute until fragrant.",
      "Add the breadcrumbs and beef broth, stir to combine, and simmer for 5 minutes until moist but holding together. Season with salt to taste and let cool.",
      "Preheat the oven to 375\u00b0F (190\u00b0C). Roll the dough out on a floured surface to about 1/8-inch thickness and cut into 8 circles, roughly 6 inches (15 cm) across.",
      "Spoon the cooled beef filling onto one half of each circle, fold the dough over to form a half-moon, and crimp the edges firmly with a fork to seal.",
      "Arrange the patties on a parchment-lined baking sheet, brush the tops with the beaten egg, and bake for 25-30 minutes until golden brown and crisp.",
      "Let cool slightly before serving."
    ],
