      "Make the filling: heat half the achiote oil in a large skillet over medium heat and cook the onion, garlic, and bell pepper until softened, about 5 minutes.",
      "Add the ground pork (traditionally diced pork shoulder, if you'd rather chop it by hand) and cook, breaking it up with a spoon, until browned, 6-8 minutes.",
      "Stir in the tomato, cumin, oregano, black pepper, and half the salt, and simmer for 8-10 minutes until thickened. Stir in the olives, capers, and raisins, then remove from the heat and let cool completely.",
      "Make the masa: peel and finely grate or food-process the green plantains, yaut\u00eda, and calabaza together until you have a smooth, thick paste.",
      "Stir the remaining achiote oil, milk, and remaining salt into the masa until it's a spreadable, evenly colored batter.",
      "Lay a piece of banana leaf (or a sheet of parchment topped with foil), about 10x12 inches/25x30 cm, lightly greased. Spread a thin, even layer of masa down the center, leaving a border, then top with a couple of tablespoons of the cooled filling.",
      "Fold the two long sides over the filling so they overlap, then fold in the ends to seal into a tight rectangular packet. Tie with kitchen twine, or wrap securely in a second layer of foil. Repeat with the remaining masa and filling to make 12 pasteles.",
      "Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil. Gently lower in the pasteles, weighing them down with a heatproof plate so they stay submerged, and boil for 45-60 minutes until the masa is firm and fully cooked.",
      "Drain and let rest for 5 minutes, then unwrap and serve hot, traditionally with hot sauce or ketchup on the side."
